[FIX] hr_work_entry: Enforce country-specific work entry types

Prior to this commit, it was possible to select generic work entry
types or work entry types belonging to other countries on various
records (leaves, allocations, resource calendars, payroll structures).

This could lead to incorrect payroll computations or leave allocations.

This commit strictly isolates work entry types based on the country
context of the relevant company or employee.

Key changes:
* Introduced `allowed_work_entry_type_ids` across multiple models to
  dynamically restrict the domain of `work_entry_type_id` fields to
  the country of the current record.
  - `res.company`
  - `hr.leave`
  - `hr.leave.allocation`
  - `resource.calendar.attendance`
  - `hr.payroll.structure.type`
  - `hr.attendance.overtime.rule`
  - etc
* Added a `post_init_hook` (`_adapt_work_entry_types_to_country`) across
  all `l10n_*_hr_payroll` modules. Upon installation, this automatically
  migrates existing generic work entry types on records (attendances,
  allocations, structure types, time off, and overtime rules) to their
  localized equivalents.
* Updated the display name of `hr.work.entry.type` to include the country
  name (or "Generic"), reducing confusion in dropdowns.
* Required `company_id` on `resource.calendar` to guarantee reliable
  country resolution.
* Set country-specific default attendance work entry types for payroll
  structure types in all localization modules.
* Removed the demo `resource_calendar_std_38h` in favor of the standard
  `resource_calendar_std` and updated related demo data across `hr`,
  `sale_timesheet`, and `planning`.

closes odoo/odoo#258600

